      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <!-- Tab 2: Habitat Overlap                  -->
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <widget class="QWidget" name="habitatTab">
       <attribute name="title">
        <string>Habitat Overlap</string>
       </attribute>
       <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="habitatTabLayout">
        <property name="leftMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="topMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="rightMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="bottomMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="habitatComingSoonLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Coming soon: Habitat &amp; Sensitive Species Overlap

This tool will intersect the trail corridor against loaded sensitive area layers (NSO habitat, Critical Habitat, Riparian Reserves, spotted frog areas, pond turtle sites, etc.) and generate a summary table for Biological Evaluations and the LAA Pre-reporting document.

Load your USFS corporate GIS layers into the project, then return here to run the overlap analysis.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="wordWrap">
           <bool>true</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="alignment">
           <set>Qt::AlignTop|Qt::AlignLeft</set>
          </property>
          <property name="styleSheet">
           <string>color: #555; padding: 8px;</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="habitatSpacer">
          <property name="orientation">
           <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
          </property>
          <property name="sizeType">
           <enum>QSizePolicy::Expanding</enum>
          </property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
           <size>
            <width>0</width>
            <height>0</height>
           </size>
          </property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <!-- Tab 3: NEPA Report                      -->
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <widget class="QWidget" name="reportTab">
       <attribute name="title">
        <string>NEPA Report</string>
       </attribute>
       <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="reportTabLayout">
        <property name="leftMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="topMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="rightMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <property name="bottomMargin">
         <number>6</number>
        </property>
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="reportComingSoonLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Coming soon: Submit for NEPA Review

This tool will package your trail design data into a standardized NEPA submission including:

  • Trail alignment shapefiles segmented by habitat type and land management allocation
  • Stream crossing point shapefile (with stream class attributes)
  • Sensitive area overlap summary table
  • Trail statistics: length by allocation, crossings by stream class, miles in Riparian Reserve
  • IMBA difficulty classification summary

Complete the Profile &amp; Difficulty and Stream Crossings analyses first, then return here to generate the report package.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="wordWrap">
           <bool>true</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="alignment">
           <set>Qt::AlignTop|Qt::AlignLeft</set>
          </property>
          <property name="styleSheet">
           <string>color: #555; padding: 8px;</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="reportSpacer">
          <property name="orientation">
           <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
          </property>
          <property name="sizeType">
           <enum>QSizePolicy::Expanding</enum>
          </property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
           <size>
            <width>0</width>
            <height>0</height>
           </size>
          </property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
